description:
For a categorical dataset, one whose template declares `classes`, such as heat stress or hazard levels or land cover. Loads the class dataset over a time range and a population dataset for one year, resamples the classes onto the population grid by nearest neighbour, and sums the people in each class within each GeoJSON feature (e.g. a DHIS2 organisation unit). The result has one row per feature, class and time step, with the class code and its label. Counts are of people at each class, not at or above it; for ordered levels, sum the higher classes to get 'at or above'.

Usage — call this process as the result of a process graph:

{
  "districts": {
    "process_id": "load_features",
    "arguments": { "id": "districts" }
  },
  "people": {
    "process_id": "population_per_class",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "heat_stress_levels_daily",
      "dataset_time": ["2026-01-01", "2026-01-31"],
      "population_dataset_id": "worldpop_population_global2_100m",
      "population_time": ["2025-01-01", "2025-12-31"],
      "geometries": { "from_node": "districts" }
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
